    .desc = A modified helmet to allow space pirates to intimidate their customers whilst staying safe from the void. Comes with some additional protection.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadHelmetSpaceSyndicateBlackEngie = black engineering space helmet
    .desc = Has a tag on it: Totally not property of an enemy corporation, honest!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadHelmetSpaceSyndicateOrange = orange space helmet
    .desc = Has a tag on it: Totally not property of an enemy corporation, honest!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadHelmetSwat = SWAT helmet
    .desc = An extremely robust, space-worthy helmet in a nefarious red and black stripe pattern.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadHoodedCarpHood = carp hood
    .desc = A hood attached to a carp costume.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadPlaybunnyearsMiner = shaft miner's bunny ears
    .desc = Muddy gray bunny ears attached to a headband. Has zero resistance against the hostile lavaland atmosphere.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadSecurityGarrison = security garrison cap
    .desc = A robust garrison cap with the security insignia emblazoned on it. Uses reinforced fabric to offer sufficient protection.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadSoftBlack = black cap
    .desc = It's a baseball hat in a tasteless black colour.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadSoftFishingHat = legendary fishing hat
    .desc = An ancient relic of a bygone era of bountiful catches and endless rivers. Printed on the front is a poem:\nWomen Fear Me\nFish Fear Me\nMen Turn Their Eyes Away From Me\nAs I Walk No Beast Dares Make A Sound In My Presence\nI Am Alone On This Barren Earth.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadSoftGreen = green cap
    .desc = It's a baseball hat in a tasteless green colour.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadSoftMime = white cap
    .desc = It's a baseball hat in a tasteless white colour.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadUtilityChefhat = chef's hat
    .desc = The commander in chef's head wear.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadUtilityHardhat = hard hat
    .desc = A piece of headgear used in dangerous working conditions to protect the head. Comes with a built-in flashlight.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadUtilityHardhatRed = firefighter helmet
    .desc = A piece of headgear used in dangerous working conditions to protect the head. Comes with a built-in flashlight.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadUtilityHardhatWeldingUp = welding hard hat
    .desc = A piece of headgear used in dangerous working conditions to protect the head. Comes with a built-in flashlight AND welding shield! The bulb seems a little smaller though.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadUtilityHardhatWeldingWhiteUp = welding hard hat
    .desc = A piece of headgear used in dangerous working conditions to protect the head. Comes with a built-in flashlight AND welding shield!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingHeadUtilityWelding = welding helmet
    .desc = A head-mounted face cover designed to protect the wearer completely from space-arc eye.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskAnimalSmallBearCursed = bear mask
    .desc = A mask made of soft vinyl and latex, representing the head of a bear.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskBalaclavaadjust = adjustable balaclava
    .desc = Wider eyed and made of an elastic based material, this one seems like it can contort more.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskBreath = breath mask
    .desc = A close-fitting mask that can be connected to an air supply.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskBreathMedical = medical mask
    .desc = A close-fitting sterile mask that can be connected to an air supply.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskFacehuggerDead = alien
    .desc = It has some sort of a tube at the end of its tail.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskGas = gas mask
    .desc = A face-covering mask that can be connected to an air supply. Good for concealing your identity and with a filter slot to help remove those toxins.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskGasAlt = gas mask
    .desc = A face-covering mask that can be connected to an air supply. Good for concealing your identity and with a filter slot to help remove those toxins.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskGasClownHat = clown wig and mask
    .desc = A true prankster's facial attire. A clown is incomplete without his wig and mask.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskGasExplorer = explorer gas mask
    .desc = A military-grade gas mask that can be connected to an air supply.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskGasHecu2 = M40 gas mask
    .desc = A deprecated field protective mask developed during the 20th century in Sol-3. It's designed to protect from chemical agents, biological agents, and nuclear fallout particles. It does not protect the user from ammonia or from lack of oxygen, though the filter can be replaced with a tube for any air tank.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskGasSechailer = security gas mask
    .desc = A standard issue Security gas mask with integrated 'Compli-o-nator 3000' device. Plays over a dozen pre-recorded compliance phrases designed to get scumbags to stand still whilst you tase them. Do not tamper with the device.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskGasSechailerSwat = SWAT mask
    .desc = A close-fitting tactical mask with an especially aggressive Compli-o-nator 3000.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskGasSeva = SEVA mask
    .desc = A head-covering mask that can be connected to an external air supply. Intended for use with the SEVA Suit.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskGasSyndicate = syndicate mask
    .desc = A close-fitting tactical mask that can be connected to an air supply.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskMadnessMask = abyssal mask
    .desc = A mask created from suffering. When you look into its eyes, it looks back.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskPartyHorn = party horn
    .desc = A paper tube used at parties that makes a noise when blown into.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingMaskSurgical = sterile mask
    .desc = A sterile mask designed to help prevent the spread of diseases.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingNeckBeads = plastic bead necklace
    .desc = A cheap, plastic bead necklace. Show team spirit! Collect them! Throw them away! The possibilities are endless!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingNeckBowtie = bow tie
    .desc = A small neosilk bowtie.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingNeckHereticFocus = amber focus
    .desc = An amber focusing glass that provides a link to the world beyond. The necklace seems to twitch, but only when you look at it from the corner of your eye.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingNeckLargeScarfSyndie = suspicious looking striped scarf
    .desc = Ready to operate.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingNeckNecklaceDope = gold necklace
    .desc = Damn, it feels good to be a gangster.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingNeckPetcollar = pet collar
    .desc = It's for pets.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingNeckStethoscope = stethoscope
    .desc = An outdated medical apparatus for listening to the sounds of the human body. It also makes you look like you know what you're doing.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingNeckTieBunnytieMiner = shaft miner's bowtie
    .desc = A purple tie that includes a collar. Looking hardy!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesClownShoes = clown shoes
    .desc = The prankster's standard-issue clowning shoes. Damn, they're huge! Ctrl-click to toggle waddle dampeners.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesClownShoesBananaShoes = mk-honk prototype shoes
    .desc = Lost prototype of advanced clown tech. Powered by bananium, these shoes leave a trail of chaos in their wake.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesCombat = combat boots
    .desc = High speed, low drag combat boots.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesCookflops = grilling sandals
    .desc = All this talk of antags, greytiding, and griefing... I just wanna grill for god's sake!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesJackboots = jackboots
    .desc = Nanotrasen-issue Security combat boots for combat scenarios or combat situations. All combat, all the time.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesJackbootsSec = security jackboots
    .desc = Lopland's Peacekeeper-issue Security combat boots for combat scenarios or combat situations. All combat, all the time.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesLaceup = laceup shoes
    .desc = The height of fashion, and they're pre-polished!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesMagboots = magboots
    .desc = Magnetic boots, often used during extravehicular activity to ensure the user remains safely attached to the vehicle.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesPirateArmored = pirate boots
    .desc = Yarr.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesSandal = sandals
    .desc = A pair of rather plain wooden sandals.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesSandalBeach = flip-flops
    .desc = A very fashionable pair of flip-flops.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesSneakersBlack = black shoes
    .desc = A pair of black shoes.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesSneakersBrown = brown shoes
    .desc = A pair of brown shoes.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesSneakersWhite = white shoes
    .desc = Comfortable-looking shoes.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesWinterboots = winter boots
    .desc = Boots lined with 'synthetic' animal fur.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesWorkboots = work boots
    .desc = Nanotrasen-issue Engineering lace-up work boots for the especially blue-collar.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesWorkbootsMining = mining boots
    .desc = Steel-toed mining boots for mining in hazardous environments. Very good at keeping toes uncrushed.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingShoesWorkbootsMiningHeeled = heeled mining boots
    .desc = Steel-toed mining heels for mining in hazardous environments. This was an awful idea.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitApronChef = cook's apron
    .desc = A basic, dull, white chef's apron.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitApronOveralls = coveralls
    .desc = A set of overalls, good for protecting thinner clothes from the elements.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitArmorBulletproof = bulletproof armor
    .desc = A Type-III-AD-P heavy bulletproof vest that excels in protecting the wearer against traditional projectile weaponry and explosives to a minor extent.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitArmorHosTrenchcoat = armored trenchcoat
    .desc = A trenchcoat enhanced with a special lightweight kevlar. The epitome of tactical plainclothes.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitArmorMilitia = station defender's coat
    .desc = A well worn uniform used by militia across the frontier, its thick padding useful for cushioning blows.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitArmorVest = armor vest
    .desc = A slim Type I armored vest that provides decent protection against most types of damage.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitArmorVestAlt = armor vest
    .desc = A Type I armored vest that provides decent protection against most types of damage.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitArmorVestAltSec = armored security vest
    .desc = A Type-II-AD-P armored vest that provides decent protection against most types of damage.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitArmorVestCapcarapaceSyndicate = syndicate captain's vest
    .desc = A sinister looking vest of advanced armor worn over a black and red fireproof jacket. The gold collar and shoulders denote that this belongs to a high ranking syndicate officer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitArmorVestCinSurplusVest = GZ-03 armor vest
    .desc = An outdated armor vest previously used by CIN military forces. The design dates back to the years leading up to CIN - TerraGov border war, and was in service until the advent of VOSKHOD powered armor becoming standard issue.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitArmorVestHecu = combat vest
    .desc = Vest designed to take heavy beating and probably keep the user alive in the process.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitBioSuitVirology = bio suit
    .desc = A suit that protects against biological contamination.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitCaution = wet floor sign
    .desc = Caution! Wet Floor!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitCostumeHawaiian = hawaiian overshirt
    .desc = A cool shirt for chilling on the beach.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitCostumePirateArmored = pirate coat
    .desc = Yarr.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitCostumePirateCaptainArmored = pirate captain coat
    .desc = Yarr.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitHoodedCarpCostume = carp costume
    .desc = A costume made from 'synthetic' carp scales, it smells.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitHoodedCultrobesEldritch = ominous armor
    .desc = A ragged, dusty set of robes. Strange eyes line the inside.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitHoodedExplorer = explorer suit
    .desc = An armoured suit for exploring harsh environments.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitHoodedExplorerExplorerharness = explorer suit harness
    .desc = An armored harness for those who are more daring than others or just like to show off the goods as they mine.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitHoodedSeva = SEVA suit
    .desc = A fire-proof suit for exploring hot environments. Its design doesn't allow for upgrading with goliath plates.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitHoodedWintercoat = winter coat
    .desc = A heavy jacket made from 'synthetic' animal furs.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitHoodedWintercoatMiner = mining winter coat
    .desc = A dusty button up winter coat. The zipper tab looks like a tiny pickaxe.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitJacketLeatherBiker = biker jacket
    .desc = You think I'm not even worth a single dollar, but I feel like a millionare.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitJacketLeatherTrenchcoat = leather trenchcoat
    .desc = A long, black trenchcoat. Makes you feel like you're the one, but you're not.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitJacketLetterman = letterman jacket
    .desc = A classic brown letterman jacket. Looks pretty hot and heavy.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitJacketLettermanNanotrasen = blue letterman jacket
    .desc = A blue letterman jacket with a proud Nanotrasen N on the back. The tag says that it was made in Space China.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitJacketLettermanRed = red letterman jacket
    .desc = A letterman jacket in a sick red color. Radical.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitJacketLettermanSyndie = blood-red letterman jacket
    .desc = Oddly, this jacket seems to have a large S on the back...

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitJacketMiljacket = military jacket
    .desc = A canvas jacket styled after classical American military garb. Feels sturdy, yet comfortable.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitJacketTailcoatMiner = explorer tailcoat
    .desc = An adapted explorer suit worn by bunny themed shaft miners. It has attachment points for goliath plates but comparatively little armor.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitSpace = space suit
    .desc = A suit that protects against low pressure environments. Has a big 13 on the back.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitSpaceEva = EVA suit
    .desc = A lightweight space suit with the basic ability to protect the wearer from the vacuum of space during emergencies.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitSpaceNasavoidOld = Engineering Voidsuit
    .desc = A CentCom engineering dark red space suit. Age has degraded the suit making it difficult to move around in.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitSpacePirate = modified EVA suit
    .desc = A modified suit to allow space pirates to board shuttles and stations while avoiding the maw of the void. Comes with additional protection and is lighter to move in.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitSpaceSyndicateBlackEngie = black engineering space suit
    .desc = Has a tag on it: Totally not property of an enemy corporation, honest!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitSpaceSyndicateOrange = orange space suit
    .desc = Has a tag on it: Totally not property of an enemy corporation, honest!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitToggleJacketZubberBomberMining = mining bomber jacket
    .desc = For a second, you swore this had a hood. Must be your brain playing tricks. You can glue plates onto it, too!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitToggleLabcoat = labcoat
    .desc = A suit that protects against minor chemical spills.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitToggleLabcoatCmo = chief medical officer's labcoat
    .desc = Bluer than the standard model.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingSuitUtilityFireFirefighter = emergency firesuit
    .desc = A suit that helps protect against fire and heat.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderAbductor = alien jumpsuit
    .desc = The most advanced form of jumpsuit known to reality, looks uncomfortable.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderColorBlack = black jumpsuit
    .desc = A standard issue colored jumpsuit. Variety is the spice of life!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderColorGrey = grey jumpsuit
    .desc = A tasteful grey jumpsuit that reminds you of the good old days.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderCostumeButtondownSlacksService = button-down shirt with slacks
    .desc = A fancy button-down shirt with slacks.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderCostumeJabroni = jabroni outfit
    .desc = The leather club is two sectors down.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderCostumeLobster = foam lobster suit
    .desc = Who beheaded the college mascot?

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderCostumePirate = pirate outfit
    .desc = Yarr.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderCostumeSailor = sailor suit
    .desc = Skipper's in the wardroom drinkin' gin.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderPantsJeans = jeans
    .desc = A nondescript pair of tough jeans.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderRankCargoMinerBunnysuit = shaft miner's bunny suit
    .desc = The staple of any bunny themed shaft miners. The perfect outfit for fighting demons on an ash choked hell planet.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderRankCargoMinerLavaland = shaft miner's jumpsuit
    .desc = A grey uniform for operating in hazardous environments.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderRankCivilianClown = clown suit
    .desc = 'HONK!'

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderRankEngineeringChiefEngineer = chief engineer's jumpsuit
    .desc = It's a high visibility jumpsuit given to those engineers insane enough to achieve the rank of "Chief Engineer". Made from fire resistant materials.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderRankEngineeringEngineer = engineer's jumpsuit
    .desc = It's an orange high visibility jumpsuit worn by engineers. Made from fire resistant materials.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderRankMedicalChiefMedicalOfficer = chief medical officer's jumpsuit
    .desc = It's a jumpsuit worn by those with the experience to be "Chief Medical Officer". It provides minor biological protection.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderRankMedicalDoctor = medical doctor's jumpsuit
    .desc = It's made of a special fiber that provides minor protection against biohazards. It has a cross on the chest denoting that the wearer is trained medical personnel.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderRankSecurityHeadOfSecurity = head of security's uniform
    .desc = A security jumpsuit decorated for those few with the dedication to achieve the position of Head of Security.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderRankSecurityOfficer = security uniform
    .desc = A tactical security uniform for officers, complete with a Lopland belt buckle.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderRankSecurityOfficerHecu = urban camouflage BDU
    .desc = A baggy military camouflage uniform with an ERDL pattern. The range of whites and greys proves useful in urban environments.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderShortsBlack = athletic shorts
    .desc = 95% Polyester, 5% Spandex!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderShortsBlue = athletic shorts
    .desc = 95% Polyester, 5% Spandex!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderShortsGreen = athletic shorts
    .desc = 95% Polyester, 5% Spandex!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderShortsGrey = athletic shorts
    .desc = 95% Polyester, 5% Spandex!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderShortsPurple = athletic shorts
    .desc = 95% Polyester, 5% Spandex!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderShortsRed = athletic shorts
    .desc = 95% Polyester, 5% Spandex!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderSuitBlackReally = executive suit
    .desc = A formal black suit, intended for the station's finest.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderSyndicate = tactical turtleneck
    .desc = A nondescript and slightly suspicious looking turtleneck with digital camouflage cargo pants.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderSyndicateCombat = combat uniform
    .desc = With a suit lined with this many pockets, you are ready to operate.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderSyndicateRusArmyCinSurplusForest = CIN combat uniform
    .desc = A CIN designed combat uniform that can come in any number of camouflauge variations. Despite this particular design being developed in the years leading up to the CIN-TerraGov border war, the uniform is still in use by many member states to this day.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderSyndicateSkirt = tactical skirtleneck
    .desc = A nondescript and slightly suspicious looking skirtleneck.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemClothingUnderSyndicateTacticool = tacticool turtleneck
    .desc = A snug turtleneck, in fabulous Nanotrasen-blue. Just looking at it makes you want to buy a NT-certifed coffee, go into the office, and -work-.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemCrowbarLargeEmergency = emergency crowbar
    .desc = It's a bulky crowbar. It almost seems deliberately designed to not be able to fit inside of a backpack.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemDualsaberGreen = double-bladed energy sword
    .desc = Handle with care.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemEncryptionkeyHeadsetMining = mining radio encryption key
    .desc = An encryption key for a radio headset.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemEtherealballdeployer = portable ethereal disco ball
    .desc = Press the button for a deployment of slightly-unethical PARTY!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemEvidencebag = evidence bag
    .desc = An empty evidence bag.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemExtinguisher = fire extinguisher
    .desc = A traditional red fire extinguisher.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemExtinguisherMini = pocket fire extinguisher
    .desc = A light and compact fibreglass-framed model fire extinguisher.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemExtractionPack = fulton extraction pack
    .desc = A balloon that can be used to extract equipment or personnel to a Fulton Recovery Beacon. Anything not bolted down can be moved. Link the pack to a beacon by using the pack in hand.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFlashlightFlareCandleInfinite = eternal candle
    .desc = In Greek myth, Prometheus stole fire from the Gods and gave it to humankind. The jewelry he kept for himself.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFlashlightFlareTorch = torch
    .desc = A torch fashioned from some leaves and a log.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFlashlightPen = penlight
    .desc = A pen-sized light, used by medical staff. It can also be used to create a hologram to alert people of incoming medical assistance.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFlashlightPenParamedic = paramedic penlight
    .desc = A high-powered UV penlight intended to help stave off infection in the field on serious burned patients. Probably really bad to look into.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFlashlightSeclite = seclite
    .desc = A robust flashlight used by security.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFoodDonkpocketWarm = warm Donk-pocket
    .desc = The heated food of choice for the seasoned traitor.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFoodGrownBanana = banana
    .desc = It's an excellent prop for a clown.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFoodGrownCarrot = carrot
    .desc = It's good for the eyes!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFoodMeatSlabMonkey = monkey meat
    .desc = A slab of meat.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFoodPieCream = banana cream pie
    .desc = Just like back home, on clown planet! HONK!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFoodPizzasliceDank = dank pizza slice
    .desc = So good, man...

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemFultonCore = extraction beacon assembly kit
    .desc = When built, emits a signal which fulton recovery devices can lock onto. Activate in hand to unfold into a beacon.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGrenadeC4X4 = X-4 charge
    .desc = A shaped high-explosive breaching charge. Designed to ensure user safety and wall nonsafety.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGrenadeChemGrenadeCleaner = cleaner grenade
    .desc = BLAM!-brand foaming space cleaner. In a special applicator for rapid cleaning of wide areas.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGrenadeChemGrenadeClf3 = clf3 grenade
    .desc = BURN!-brand foaming clf3. In a special applicator for rapid purging of wide areas.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGrenadeChemGrenadeSmartMetalFoam = smart metal foam grenade
    .desc = Used for emergency sealing of hull breaches, while keeping areas accessible.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGrenadeMirage = mirage grenade
    .desc = A special device that, when activated, produces a holographic copy of the user.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGrenadeSmokebomb = smoke grenade
    .desc = Real bruh moment if you ever see this. Probably tell a c*der or something.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticAr = NT-ARG 'Boarder'
    .desc = A robust assault rifle used by Nanotrasen fighting forces.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticC20rUnrestricted = C-20r SMG
    .desc = A bullpup three-round burst .45 SMG, designated 'C-20r'. Has a 'Scarborough Arms - Per falcis, per pravitas' buttstamp.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticL6SawUnrestricted = L6 SAW
    .desc = A heavily modified 7mm light machine gun, designated 'L6 SAW'. Has 'Aussec Armoury - 2531' engraved on the receiver below the designation.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticLanca = Lanca Battle Rifle
    .desc = A relatively compact, long barreled bullpup battle rifle chambered for .310 Strilka. Has an integrated sight with a surprisingly functional amount of magnification, given its place of origin.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticMiecz = Miecz Submachine Gun
    .desc = A short barrel, further compacted conversion of the 'Lanca' rifle to fire pistol caliber .27-54 cartridges. Due to the intended purpose of the weapon, and less than optimal ranged performance of the projectile, it has nothing more than basic glow-sights as opposed to the ranged scope Lanca users might be used to.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticMiniUzi = Type U3 Uzi
    .desc = A lightweight, burst-fire submachine gun, for when you really want someone dead. Uses 9mm rounds.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticPistol = Makarov pistol
    .desc = A small, easily concealable 9x25mm Mk.12 handgun. Has a threaded barrel for suppressors.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticPistolAps = Stechkin APS machine pistol
    .desc = A modernized reproduction of an old Soviet machine pistol. It fires quickly, but kicks like a mule. Uses 9mm ammo. Has a threaded barrel for suppressors.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticPistolDeagle = Desert Eagle
    .desc = A robust .50 AE handgun.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticPistolPlasmaMarksman = Gwiazda Plasma Sharpshooter
    .desc = An outdated sidearm rarely seen in use by some members of the CIN. Uses plasma power packs. Fires relatively accurate globs of searing plasma.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticPistolPlasmaThrower = Słońce Plasma Projector
    .desc = An outdated sidearm rarely seen in use by some members of the CIN. Uses plasma power packs. Spews an inaccurate stream of searing plasma out the magnetic barrel so long as it has power and the trigger is pulled.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticPistolSol = Wespe Pistol
    .desc = The standard issue service pistol of TerraGov's various military branches. Uses .35 Sol and comes with an attached light.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticSolSmg = Sindano Submachine Gun
    .desc = A small submachine gun firing .35 Sol. Commonly seen in the hands of PMCs and other unsavory corpos. Accepts any standard Sol pistol magazine.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticWt550 = WT-550 Autorifle
    .desc = Recalled by Nanotrasen due to public backlash around heat distribution resulting in unintended discombobulation. This outcry was fabricated through various Syndicate-backed misinformation operations to force Nanotrasen to abandon its ballistics weapon program, cornering them into the energy weapons market. Most often found today in the hands of pirates, underfunded security personnel, cargo technicians, theoretical physicists, and gang bangers out on the rim. Light-weight and fully automatic. Uses 4.6x30mm rounds.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticAutomaticWylom = Wyłom Anti-Materiel Rifle
    .desc = A massive, outdated beast of an anti materiel rifle that was once in use by CIN military forces. Fires the devastating .60 Strela caseless round, the massively overperforming penetration of which being the reason this weapon was discontinued.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticRevolver = .357 revolver
    .desc = A suspicious revolver. Uses .357 ammo.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticRevolverC38 = .38 revolver
    .desc = A classic, if not outdated, lethal firearm. Uses .38 Special rounds.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticRevolverGolden = Golden revolver
    .desc = This ain't no game, ain't never been no show, And I'll gladly gun down the oldest lady you know. Uses .357 ammo.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticRevolverMateba = Unica 6 auto-revolver
    .desc = A retro high-powered autorevolver typically used by officers of the New Russia military. Uses .357 ammo.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticRevolverShotgunRevolver = Bóbr 12 GA revolver
    .desc = An outdated sidearm rarely seen in use by some members of the CIN. A revolver type design with a four shell cylinder. That's right, shell, this one shoots twelve guage.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticRifleBoltaction = Sakhno Precision Rifle
    .desc = A Sakhno Precision Rifle, a bolt action weapon that was (and certainly still is) popular with frontiersmen, cargo runners, private security forces, explorers, and other unsavoury types. This particular pattern of the rifle dates back all the way to 2440.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticRifleBoltactionSurplus = Sakhno M2442 Army
    .desc = A modification of the Sakhno Precision Rifle, "Sakhno M2442 Army" is stamped into the side. It is unknown what army this pattern of rifle was made for or if it was ever even used by an army of any sort. What you can discern, however, is that its previous owner did not treat the weapon well. For some reason, there's moisture all through the internals.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticRifleLionhunter = Lionhunter's Rifle
    .desc = An antique looking rifle that looks immaculate despite being clearly very old.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticRifleSniperRifle = anti-materiel sniper rifle
    .desc = A boltaction anti-materiel rifle, utilizing .50 BMG cartridges. While technically outdated in modern arms markets, it still works exceptionally well as an anti-personnel rifle. In particular, the employment of modern armored MODsuits utilizing advanced armor plating has given this weapon a new home on the battlefield. It is also able to be suppressed... somehow.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticRocketlauncherUnrestricted = Dardo-RE Rocket Launcher
    .desc = A reusable rocket propelled grenade launcher. An arrow pointing toward the front of the launcher alongside the words "Front Toward Enemy" are printed on the tube. A sticker near the back of the launcher warn to "CHECK BACKBLAST CLEAR BEFORE FIRING", whatever that means.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticShotgunLethal = shotgun
    .desc = A traditional shotgun with wood furniture and a four-shell capacity underneath.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunBallisticShotgunRiot = woodstock shotgun
    .desc = A sturdy shotgun with a longer magazine and a fixed tactical stock designed for non-lethal riot control. Often found in the hand of a lavaland hunter. Vaguely reminds you of hunting back in Sol does it not?

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunEnergyEGun = Allstar SC-2 energy carbine
    .desc = A basic hybrid energy carbine with two settings: disable and kill.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunEnergyEGunAdvtaser = hybrid taser
    .desc = A dual-mode taser designed to fire both short-range high-power electrodes and long-range disabler beams.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunEnergyLaser = Allstar SC-1 laser carbine
    .desc = A basic energy-based laser carbine that fires concentrated beams of light which pass through glass and thin metal.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunEnergyLaserHellgun = Type 2 'hellfire' laser gun
    .desc = The Type 2 Heat Delivery System, developed by Nanotrasen. Technically speaking, it is an improvement. Legally speaking, possession of this weapon is restricted in most occupied sectors of space. The Type 2 is notorious for its ability to render victims a carbonized husk with ease, melting flesh and bone as easily as butter. A painful, gruesome death awaits anyone on the wrong ends of this gun.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunEnergyLaserMusket = laser musket
    .desc = A hand-crafted laser weapon, it has a hand crank on the side to charge it up.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunEnergyLaserRetro = Type 1 laser gun
    .desc = The Type 1 Heat Delivery System, developed by Nanotrasen. No longer used by Nanotrasen's private security or military forces. Nevertheless, it is still quite deadly and easy to maintain, making it a favorite amongst pirates and other outlaws.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunEnergyLaserXray = Type 6 X-ray laser gun
    .desc = The Type 6 Heat Delivery System, developed by Nanotrasen. Capable of expelling concentrated 'X-ray' blasts that pass through multiple soft targets and heavier materials.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunEnergyRechargeKineticAccelerator = proto-kinetic accelerator
    .desc = A self recharging, ranged mining tool that does increased damage in low pressure.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunEnergyRechargeKineticAcceleratorMinebot = proto-kinetic accelerator
    .desc = A self recharging, ranged mining tool that does increased damage in low pressure.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunEnergyShrinkRay = shrink ray blaster
    .desc = This is a piece of frightening alien tech that enhances the magnetic pull of atoms in a localized space to temporarily make an object shrink. That or it's just space magic. Either way, it shrinks stuff.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemGunMagicStaffHonk = staff of the honkmother
    .desc = Honk.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemHatchetWooden = hatchet
    .desc = A crude axe blade upon a short wooden handle.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemInstrumentBikehorn = gilded bike horn
    .desc = An exquisitely decorated bike horn, capable of honking in a variety of notes.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemInstrumentGuitar = guitar
    .desc = It's made of wood and has bronze strings.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemInstrumentPianoSynth = synthesizer
    .desc = An advanced electronic synthesizer that can be used as various instruments.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemKineticCrusher = proto-kinetic crusher
    .desc = An early design of the proto-kinetic accelerator, it is little more than a combination of various mining tools cobbled together, forming a high-tech club. While it is an effective mining tool, it did little to aid any but the most skilled and/or suicidal miners against local fauna.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemKnifeButcher = butcher's cleaver
    .desc = A huge thing used for chopping and chopping up meat. This includes clowns and clown by-products.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemKnifeCombat = combat knife
    .desc = A military combat utility survival knife.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemKnifeCombatCyborg = cyborg knife
    .desc = A cyborg-mounted plasteel knife. Extremely sharp and durable.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemKnifeCombatSurvival = survival knife
    .desc = A hunting grade survival knife.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemKnifeEnvy = envy's knife
    .desc = Their success will be yours.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemKnifeHunting = hunting knife
    .desc = Despite its name, it's mainly used for cutting meat from dead prey rather than actual hunting.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemKnifeKitchen = kitchen knife
    .desc = A general purpose Chef's Knife made by SpaceCook Incorporated. Guaranteed to stay sharp for years to come.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemKnifeShivCarrot = carrot shiv
    .desc = Unlike other carrots, you should probably keep this far away from your eyes.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemKnifeShivPlastitanium = plastitanium shiv
    .desc = A makeshift titanium-infused plasma glass shiv.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemLaserPointerBlue = laser pointer
    .desc = Don't shine it in your eyes!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeBaseballBat = baseball bat
    .desc = There ain't a skull in the league that can withstand a swatter.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeBatonAbductor = advanced baton
    .desc = A quad-mode baton used for incapacitation and restraining of specimens.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeBatonSecurityLoaded = stun baton
    .desc = The Secure Apprehension Device, as developed by Nanotrasen. Delivers a precise shock to a target's central nervous system to incapacitate them.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeBatonSecurityLoadedHos = stun baton
    .desc = The Secure Apprehension Device, as developed by Nanotrasen. Delivers a precise shock to a target's central nervous system to incapacitate them.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeBatonTelescopicSilver = silver-capped telescopic baton
    .desc = A compact yet robust personal defense weapon. Can be concealed when folded. This one is ranked SILVER, and thus has decent penetrative power.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeChainofcommand = chain of command
    .desc = A tool used by great men to placate the frothing masses. Can be used to hasten allies with right-click.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeEnergySwordPirate = energy cutlass
    .desc = Arrrr matey.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeEnergySwordSaberRed = energy sword
    .desc = May the force be within you.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeRuneCarver = carving knife
    .desc = A small knife made of cold steel, pure and perfect. Its sharpness can carve into titanium itself - but only few can evoke the dangers that lurk beneath reality.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeSabre = officer's sabre
    .desc = An elegant weapon, its monomolecular edge is capable of cutting through flesh and bone with ease.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeSicklyBlade = sickly blade
    .desc = A sickly green crescent blade, decorated with an ornamental eye. You feel like you're being watched...

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMeleeSkateboardHoverboard = hoverboard
    .desc = A blast from the past, so retro!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemMiningVoucher = mining voucher
    .desc = A token to redeem a piece of equipment. Use it on a mining equipment vendor.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModControlPreEquippedElite = elite MOD control unit
    .desc = An elite suit upgraded by Cybersun Industries, offering upgraded armor values.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModControlPreEquippedEngineering = MOD control unit
    .desc = The control unit of a Modular Outerwear Device, a powered suit that protects against various environments.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModControlPreEquippedSecurity = MOD control unit
    .desc = The control unit of a Modular Outerwear Device, a powered suit that protects against various environments.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleEmpShield = MOD EMP shield module
    .desc = A field inhibitor installed into the suit, protecting it against feedback such as electromagnetic pulses that would otherwise damage the electronic systems of the suit or it's modules. However, it will take from the suit's power to do so.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleFlashlight = MOD flashlight module
    .desc = A simple pair of configurable flashlights installed on the left and right sides of the helmet, useful for providing light in a variety of ranges and colors. Some survivalists prefer the color green for their illumination, for reasons unknown.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleHatStabilizerSyndicate = MOD elite hat stabilizer module
    .desc = A simple set of deployable stands, directly atop one's head; these will deploy under a hat to keep it from falling off, allowing them to be worn atop the sealed helmet. You still need to take the hat off your head while the helmet deploys, though. This is a must-have for Syndicate Operatives and Agents alike, enabling them to continue to style on the opposition even while in their MODsuit.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleHearingProtection = MOD hearing protection module
    .desc = A module that protects the users ears from loud sounds

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleJetpackAdvanced = MOD advanced ion jetpack module
    .desc = An improvement on the previous model of electric thrusters. This one achieves higher precision and spartial stability through mounting of more jets and application of red paint.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleJumpJet = MOD ionic jump jet module
    .desc = A specialised ionic thruster which provides a short but powerful boost capable of pushing against gravity, after which time it needs to recharge.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleMagneticHarness = MOD magnetic harness module
    .desc = Based off old TerraGov harness kits, this magnetic harness automatically attaches dropped guns back to the wearer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleNight = MOD night vision module
    .desc = A heads-up display installed into the visor of the suit. Typical for both civilian and military applications, this allows the user to perceive their surroundings while in complete darkness, enhancing the view by tenfold; yet brightening everything into a spooky green glow. They say these also let you see behind you. These ones are a special version which remain compatible with the other visor modules.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleQuickCuff = MOD restraint assist module
    .desc = Enhanced gauntlet grip pads that help with placing individuals in restraints more quickly. Doesn't look like they'll come off.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleShockAbsorber = MOD shock absorption module
    .desc = A module that makes the user resistant to the knockdown inflicted by Stun Batons.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleStorageSyndicate = MOD syndicate storage module
    .desc = A storage system using nanotechnology developed by Cybersun Industries, these compartments use esoteric technology to compress the physical matter of items put inside of them, essentially shrinking items for much easier and more portable storage.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModModuleWeldingSyndicate = MODsuit flash-protected optical suite
    .desc = A module installed into the visor of the suit, this projects a polarized, holographic overlay in front of the user's eyes. It's rated high enough for immunity against extremities such as spot and arc welding, solar eclipses, and handheld flashlights.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModularComputerPda = pda
    .desc = A small portable microcomputer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModularComputerPdaAssistant = assistant PDA
    .desc = A small portable microcomputer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModularComputerPdaClown = clown PDA
    .desc = A small portable microcomputer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModularComputerPdaEngineering = engineering PDA
    .desc = A small portable microcomputer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModularComputerPdaHeadsCe = chief engineer PDA
    .desc = A small portable microcomputer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModularComputerPdaHeadsCmo = chief medical officer PDA
    .desc = A small portable microcomputer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModularComputerPdaHeadsHos = head of security PDA
    .desc = A small portable microcomputer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModularComputerPdaMedical = medical PDA
    .desc = A small portable microcomputer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModularComputerPdaSecurity = security PDA
    .desc = A small portable microcomputer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemModularComputerPdaShaftminer = shaft miner PDA
    .desc = A small portable microcomputer.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemPaperFluffJobsMedicalBloodTypes = blood type compatibility reference

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemPinpointerCrew = crew pinpointer
    .desc = A handheld tracking device that points to crew suit sensors.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadset = radio headset
    .desc = An updated, modular intercom that fits over the head. Takes encryption keys.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadsetHeadsCe = the chief engineer's headset
    .desc = The headset of the guy in charge of keeping the station powered and undamaged.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadsetHeadsCmo = the chief medical officer's headset
    .desc = The headset of the highly trained medical chief.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadsetHeadsHosAlt = the head of security's bowman headset
    .desc = The headset of the man in charge of keeping order and protecting the station. Protects ears from flashbangs.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadsetHeadsetCargoMining = mining radio headset
    .desc = Headset used by shaft miners. It has a mining network uplink which allows the user to quickly transmit commands to their comrades and amplifies their voice in low-pressure environments.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadsetHeadsetEng = engineering radio headset
    .desc = When the engineers wish to chat like girls.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadsetHeadsetFactionBowman = faction bowman headset
    .desc = Headset used by the faction. Protects ears from flashbangs.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadsetHeadsetMed = medical radio headset
    .desc = A headset for the trained staff of the medbay.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadsetHeadsetSecAlt = security bowman headset
    .desc = This is used by your elite security force. Protects ears from flashbangs.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadsetHeadsetSrv = service radio headset
    .desc = Headset used by the service staff, tasked with keeping the station full, happy and clean.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRadioHeadsetPsyker = psychic headset
    .desc = A headset designed to boost psychic waves. Protects ears from flashbangs.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRag = damp rag
    .desc = For cleaning up messes, you suppose.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersBlood = blood pack
    .desc = Contains blood used for transfusion. Must be attached to an IV drip.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersBloodAMinus = blood pack
    .desc = Contains blood used for transfusion. Must be attached to an IV drip.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersBloodBMinus = blood pack
    .desc = Contains blood used for transfusion. Must be attached to an IV drip.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersBloodBPlus = blood pack
    .desc = Contains blood used for transfusion. Must be attached to an IV drip.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersBloodEthereal = blood pack
    .desc = Contains blood used for transfusion. Must be attached to an IV drip.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersBloodLizard = blood pack
    .desc = Contains blood used for transfusion. Must be attached to an IV drip.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersBloodOMinus = blood pack
    .desc = Contains blood used for transfusion. Must be attached to an IV drip.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersBloodOPlus = blood pack
    .desc = Contains blood used for transfusion. Must be attached to an IV drip.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersBloodRandom = blood pack
    .desc = Contains blood used for transfusion. Must be attached to an IV drip.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersCondimentFlour = flour sack
    .desc = A big bag of flour. Good for baking!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersCondimentRice = rice sack
    .desc = A big bag of rice. Good for cooking!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersCondimentSugar = sugar sack
    .desc = Tasty spacey sugar!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersCupGlassBottleBeerLight = Carp Lite
    .desc = Brewed with "Pure Ice Asteroid Spring Water".

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersCupGlassColocup = colo cup
    .desc = A cheap, mass produced style of cup, typically used at parties. They never seem to come out red, for some reason...

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersCupGlassMugCoco = Dutch hot coco
    .desc = Made in Space South America.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersHyposprayMedipenSurvival = survival emergency medipen
    .desc = A medipen for surviving in the harsh environments, heals most common damage sources. WARNING: May cause organ damage.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemReagentContainersSprayWaterflower = water flower
    .desc = A seemingly innocent sunflower...with a twist.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemResonator = resonator
    .desc = A handheld device that creates small fields of energy that resonate until they detonate, crushing rock. It does increased damage in low pressure. It has two modes: Automatic and manual detonation.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemRestraintsHandcuffs = handcuffs
    .desc = Use this to keep prisoners in line.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStackMarkerBeacon = marker beacon
    .desc = Prism-brand path illumination devices. Used by miners to mark paths and warn of danger.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStackMarkerBeaconTen = marker beacon
    .desc = Prism-brand path illumination devices. Used by miners to mark paths and warn of danger.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStackMarkerBeaconThirty = marker beacon
    .desc = Prism-brand path illumination devices. Used by miners to mark paths and warn of danger.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStampClown = clown's rubber stamp
    .desc = A rubber stamp for stamping important documents.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStockPartsPowerStoreCellBluespace = bluespace power cell
    .desc = A rechargeable transdimensional power cell.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBackpack = backpack
    .desc = You wear this on your back and put items into it.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBackpackDuffelbag = duffel bag
    .desc = A large duffel bag for holding extra things.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBackpackDuffelbagMiningBunnyConscript = Bunny Kit
    .desc = A mining outfit kit themed around bunnies, they do live in burrows after all...

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBackpackDuffelbagMiningConscript = mining conscription kit
    .desc = A duffel bag containing everything a crewmember needs to support a shaft miner in the field.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBackpackErtOdstHecu = hecu backpack
    .desc = A modified backpack that attaches via magnetic harness, removing the need for straps.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBackpackIndustrialCinSurplusForest = CIN military backpack
    .desc = A rugged backpack often used by the CIN's military forces.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBackpackSatchel = satchel
    .desc = A trendy looking satchel.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBackpackSatchelLeatherWithwallet = leather satchel
    .desc = It's a very fancy satchel made with fine leather.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBagOre = mining satchel
    .desc = This little bugger can be used to store and transport ores.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBagTrashFilled = trash bag
    .desc = It's the heavy-duty black polymer kind. Time to take out the trash!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBeltBandolier = bandolier
    .desc = A bandolier for holding rifle shotgun, and bigger revolver caliber ammunition.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBeltChampion = championship belt
    .desc = Proves to the world that you are the strongest!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBeltMilitaryCinSurplusForest = chest rig
    .desc = A tactical webbing often used by the CIN's military forces.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBeltMiningVendor = explorer's webbing
    .desc = A versatile chest rig, cherished by miners and hunters alike.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBeltUtilityChiefFull = chief engineer's toolbelt
    .desc = Holds tools, looks snazzy.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBeltUtilityFullEngi = toolbelt
    .desc = Holds tools.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBoxBalloons = box of long balloons
    .desc = A completely randomized and wacky box of long balloons, harvested straight from balloon farms on the clown planet.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBoxBeanbag = box of shotgun shells (Less Lethal - Beanbag)
    .desc = A box full of beanbag shotgun shells, designed for shotguns.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBoxEmergencySpacesuit = emergency space suit case
    .desc = A small case containing an emergency space suit and helmet.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageBoxNriSurvivalPackRaider = PSC survival pack
    .desc = A box filled with useful emergency items, supplied by the Commonwealth. It feels particularily light.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageDice = bag of dice
    .desc = Contains all the luck you'll ever need.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageInflatable = inflatable barrier box
    .desc = Contains inflatable walls and doors.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageLunchboxBunnyCarrot = carrot lunchbox
    .desc = Who needs Mesons?

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageMedkitEmergency = emergency medkit
    .desc = A very simple first aid kit meant to secure and stabilize serious wounds for later treatment.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageMedkitSurgery = surgical medkit
    .desc = A high capacity aid kit for doctors, full of medical supplies and basic surgical equipment.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageToolboxEmergency = emergency toolbox
    .desc = Danger. Very robust.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemStorageWalletRandom = wallet
    .desc = It can hold a few small and personal things.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemSuitVoucher = suit voucher
    .desc = A token to redeem a new suit. Use it on a mining equipment vendor.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemSurvivalcapsule = bluespace shelter capsule
    .desc = An emergency shelter stored within a pocket of bluespace.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemTScanner = T-ray scanner
    .desc = A terahertz-ray emitter and scanner used to detect underfloor objects such as cables and pipes.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemTScannerAdvMiningScannerLesser = automatic mining scanner
    .desc = A scanner that automatically checks surrounding rock for useful minerals; it can also be used to stop gibtonite detonations.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemTankInternalsEmergencyOxygen = emergency oxygen tank
    .desc = Used for emergencies. Contains very little oxygen, so try to conserve it until you actually need it.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemTankInternalsOxygen = oxygen tank
    .desc = A tank of oxygen, this one is blue.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemTankInternalsOxygenRed = oxygen tank
    .desc = A tank of oxygen, this one is red.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemTankInternalsOxygenYellow = oxygen tank
    .desc = A tank of oxygen, this one is yellow.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemTankJetpackCarbondioxide = jetpack (carbon dioxide)
    .desc = A tank of compressed carbon dioxide for use as propulsion in zero-gravity areas. Painted black to indicate that it should not be used as a source for internals.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemTankJetpackHarness = jet harness (oxygen)
    .desc = A lightweight tactical harness, used by those who don't want to be weighed down by traditional jetpacks.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalAi = balloon ai core
    .desc = A somewhat unrealistic balloon effigy of the station's AI core. Actual AI probably wouldn't smile like this.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalBanana = balloon banana
    .desc = A balloon banana. This one can't be slipped on. Good for psychological warfare, though.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalCat = balloon cat
    .desc = Without the sharp claws, balloon cats are possibly cuter than their live counterparts, though not as relatable, warm and fuzzy.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalClown = balloon clown
    .desc = A balloon clown, smiling from ear to ear and beyond!

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalDog = balloon dog
    .desc = A balloon effigy of the best boy. It cannot truly compare, but it makes an effort.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalEthereal = balloon ethereal
    .desc = A balloon effigy of an ethereal artisan. Clownery is one form of art, and as such, ethereals were both drawn to and readily accepted at clown planet. Don't mind the lighbulb head, it's art too.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalFly = balloon fly
    .desc = A balloon effigy of a flyperson. Thankfully, it doesn't come with balloon vomit.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalGuy = balloon guy
    .desc = A balloon effigy of the everyday standard issue human guy. Wonder if he pays balloon taxes. He probably evades them.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalLizard = balloon lizard
    .desc = A balloon effigy of a lizard. One of the first species to adapt to clown planet's culture. Perhaps because they are naturally laughable?

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalMoth = balloon moth
    .desc = A balloon effigy of a common member of moth flotillas. Very few of them ever decide to settle on the clown planet, but those who do have the best 'piece-of-cloth-disappearing' acts.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalNukie = balloon nukie
    .desc = A balloon effigy of syndicate's nuclear operative. Either made to appease them and pray for survival, or to poke fun at them.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalPlasmaman = balloon plasmaman
    .desc = A balloon effigy of a plasmaman. Among the rarest on the clown planet, only having appeared recently thanks to ready trade between clown planet and NT.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalPodguy = balloon podguy
    .desc = A balloon effigy of a podperson. Though, actual podpeople have heads and not stalks and leaves.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalSlime = balloon slime
    .desc = A balloon effigy of single specimen of the galaxy-wide slime scourge, of purple variety. Slimes tried to invade clown planet once. They got quickly washed out by water-spitting flowers, though.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonAnimalXeno = balloon xeno
    .desc = A balloon effigy of a spooky xeno! Too squishy to scare anyone itself, though.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemToyBalloonLong = long balloon
    .desc = A perfect balloon to contort into goofy forms. Sealed with a mechanical bluespace wrap so it remains floating no matter what.

ent-BitrunSourceObjItemVendingRefillBoozeomat = resupply canister
